{
  "version": "0.7.0",
  "notes": "### Added\n- Learning items, sketches, projects, Money accounts and Vault items can each belong to an area, like tasks, notes and events. A device that syncs only some areas now shows Money, Learning, Sketches and Vault with just those areas.\n- Money areas are set per account. An account's entries and linked goals follow it. A transfer between areas is counted once on your full devices, and a device with only one side still shows the right balance.\n- Each area's Vault items are in their own encrypted file, opened with the same password. A work device can open only its areas' items.\n- Area chips and filters in Learning, Sketches, Projects, Money and Vault, and an area picker when adding or editing.\n- When the folder you pick for your workspace already has other files, Pyxida suggests a Pyxida folder inside it.\n- The setup preview counts every kind of item per area.\n\n### Changed\n- New area types turn on once every device runs this version. Until then Pyxida lists the devices to update and lets you continue anyway.\n- Projects without an area move to Personal during that upgrade, so no device loses them. Afterwards, a project with no area stays on full devices only.\n- On Windows, Sync data is kept in this computer's local app data instead of the roaming profile.\n- A device that syncs only some areas cannot set up a new Vault; set it up on a device with every area.\n\n### Fixed\n- An image used by notes in different areas now reaches each of those areas.\n- Switching a device to full no longer lists conflicts for notes that moved into an area.",
